q1: Janaka asks how Knowledge can be acquired
q2: Janaka asks how Liberation can come
q3: Janaka asks how renunciation can be achieved
q4: Aspiring for Liberation calls for rejecting objects of the senses as poison
q5: Aspiring for Liberation calls for seeking forgiveness, straightforwardness, kindness, cheerfulness, and truth as nectar
q6: You are neither earth, water, fire, air, nor space
q7: Freedom is attained by knowing Self as witness of all these and embodiment of pure Consciousness
q8: Detaching from body and abiding in Consciousness makes you immediately happy, peaceful, and free from bondage
q9: You belong to neither Brāhmaṇa, caste, nor station in life (āśrama)
q10: You are not perceivable by the senses
q11: Being unattached, formless, and witness of all, be happy
